INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line monthly sales volume relative to its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combinations with their ratios, months, and return rates, and assess whether each spike is real demand or channel stuffing. Output a Markdown report saved to disk with full source annotations.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute monthly volume vs 24-month mean ratio: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) group, compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24_month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_ratio_analysis.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the ratio CSV, find the top-3 (region × product_line × month) combinations with the highest volume-to-mean ratio. For each, also extract the return rate (退货率) for that specific month from the original CSV. Save a small summary table to offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv → code_agent
4. Assess real demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate trend in the 3 months before/after the spike, (b) whether the spike is a single-month spike or sustained, (c) compare with the same product_line's other regions in the same month. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/anomaly_assessment.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing top-3 anomalies with ratio, month, return rate; (3) every key number annotated with source in format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging real demand vs channel stuffing for each anomaly; (5) all conclusions derived solely from the local CSV. Embed the assessment table and any relevant charts as inline Markdown tables (no external image files needed, but if code_agent generates a chart PNG, embed it with relative path). → code_agent
